1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Who selects:** Under Section 32(a) of the Investment Company Act of 1940, the trust's board selects the independent public accountant by majority vote, including a majority of the independent trustees. The vote must occur within 30 days before or after the fiscal year begins, or before the annual shareholder meeting. For exchange-listed ETFs, Exchange Act Rule 10A-3 and listing standards also require an independent audit committee that directly appoints and oversees the auditor.\n\n**When ratification can be omitted:**\n1. **No annual meeting.** Section 32(a) requires ratification only at the next annual meeting \"if such meeting is held.\" Most Delaware and Massachusetts trusts hold none, so the issue rarely arises.\n2. **Rule 32a-4 exemption.** Ratification is unnecessary if the fund has:\n   - an audit committee of only independent trustees,\n   - a board-adopted committee charter, kept as a record, and\n   - committee oversight of the auditor.\n\nThe board and committee still select and terminate the auditor.","ttft_ms":845,"type":"result","duration_ms":3317,"uuid":"8ef25b88-1873-46e4-be53-d91f75362f15","ttft_stream_ms":640,"time_to_request_ms":58,"first_content_frame_ms":641,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
